# Search Index Sync

Whenever you create, rename, or delete a page under `frontend/app/(site)/`, you **must** update `frontend/lib/search-index.ts` in the same change.

## What to update

Each entry in `SEARCH_INDEX` maps to one page:

```ts
{
  path: "/our-solutions/affiliates/",   // URL path, trailing slash required
  title: "Affiliates",                  // Human-readable title (without "| AmeriLife")
  description: "...",                   // Page meta description
  keywords: ["partnership", "network"], // 3–8 key topics from the page content
}
```

## Rules

- **New page** → add a new entry. Use the `metadata.description` export (or the page's `<h1>` / opening paragraph if there is no metadata).
- **Deleted page** → remove its entry.
- **Renamed/moved page** → update the `path` field.
- Exclude utility/redirect pages that have no real content: `thankyou`, `findanagentthankyou`, `about/affiliates/thank-you`, `test`, `existinglead`, `worksite/lead`, `connect`, `broker-contact-page`, `sma-amerilife-video`, `valspar`, `sms-terms`.
- `path` must be the actual Next.js route, e.g. `app/(site)/our-solutions/affiliates/page.tsx` → `/our-solutions/affiliates/`.
- **Blog posts** are not in this index: they come from WordPress (GraphQL) and are searched automatically on the search page. Only add static Next.js pages here.
